<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>x09 Group Policy Templates - Ansible</displayName>
  <description>Group Policy Templates for Ansible Management</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="AnsiblePlaybook_Name">Ansible Playbook Management</string>
      <string id="AnsiblePlaybook_Explain">Configure Ansible playbook execution on client machines.

This policy allows you to specify the filename of an Ansible playbook that will be executed on the target system when Group Policy is applied.

Playbook filename:
Specify the playbook filename (e.g., configure_system.yml). The file must be located in the Machine/Scripts/YML subfolder of the policy directory.

The playbook will be executed automatically when Group Policy is updated.

Ensure that the playbook file is accessible for reading on the target system and contains valid YAML syntax.</string>
      <string id="PlaybookFilename_Name">Playbook filename</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="AnsiblePlaybook">
        <textBox refId="PlaybookFilename">
          <label>Playbook filename:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
